{"id": "EUVD-2026-103829", "enisaUuid": "0406343d-934c-3154-bf7a-2f9ffb2b5aae", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: codecs: max98363: fix uninitialized stream_config->type\n\nstream_config is not initialized before being passed to\nsdw_stream_add_slave().  The type field may contain garbage and is\nlater copied to stream->type by sdw_config_stream().\n\nZero-initialize stream_config so type defaults to SDW_STREAM_PCM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a756c93fae312cc2bcdf157a0992e505573c530f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c251426bb67de5cbfd3b5550bd5983736e8b9c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7df8c39a50f364c04d68881e61ba1ecad29d4b72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f44ba04c7a32bd13dbdcd814385b8629d0ee95e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bcd61aa247c28b721ac21dda6e4135f75a2de29f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5h63-gmxc-wv3q", "CVE-2026-98744"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2aeb5c91-033c-3768-8634-1b1b635af989", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "18c0af945fa35766730d3f729adcf417a3d1ad5d <a756c93fae312cc2bcdf157a0992e505573c530f"}, {"id": "2e1c2720-0123-3dd2-8dcc-265cf27e8c4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "31fc4e1f-9dd0-3c2a-b7a0-f91ffae1d342", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4322a05d-5fda-34f8-b829-1ec6d6dccb2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "522f30b5-3159-3c78-9a23-bce60a5ef7f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "539736d0-b4e6-3d20-b4ab-bc1bb812ad2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "18c0af945fa357